{%- comment -%}
  California Proposition 65 warning.

  WHY THIS EXISTS: Prop 65 follows the product, not the business. Any online
  seller whose goods reach a California consumer is covered, wherever the seller
  is. Since the 2016 OEHHA e-commerce rules, the warning must appear **on the
  product display page** — as a clearly marked hyperlink or a displayed warning —
  and must be seen *before* the purchase is completed. Penalties run to $2,500 per
  day per violation, and Prop 65 is enforced largely by private bounty-hunter
  plaintiffs who scan storefronts, which is why imported goods sold online are a
  favourite target.

  Imported foot-care goods are squarely in scope: flexible PVC and gel components
  commonly contain DEHP and other listed phthalates, and some plastics and metal
  fittings carry lead.

  HOW TO USE IT: this is driven per product by metafields, because whether a
  warning is required depends on the item and its actual materials — it is not a
  sitewide toggle, and a blanket "everything is warned" is its own risk.

    custom.prop65_required   boolean         — show the warning for this product
    custom.prop65_chemical   single line     — the listed chemical, e.g. "DEHP"
    custom.prop65_type       single line     — "cancer", "reproductive harm", or
                                               "cancer and reproductive harm"

  Renders nothing unless prop65_required is true. Under the amendments effective
  January 2025 a short-form warning must name at least one chemical, so if no
  chemical is supplied this falls back to the long-form wording, which does not
  require one.

  Ask your supplier for the Prop 65 status and any test reports for each SKU
  before deciding. Do not guess in either direction.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign required = product.metafields.custom.prop65_required
  assign chemical = product.metafields.custom.prop65_chemical | metafield_text | strip
  assign harm = product.metafields.custom.prop65_type | metafield_text | strip | downcase
  if harm == blank
    assign harm = 'cancer and reproductive harm'
  endif
-%}

{%- if required == true -%}
  <details class="sw-prop65" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    <summary class="sw-prop65__summary">
      <span class="sw-prop65__mark" aria-hidden="true">&#9888;</span>
      <span class="sw-prop65__label">
        <strong>WARNING:</strong> California Proposition 65
      </span>
    </summary>
    <div class="sw-prop65__body">
      {%- if chemical != blank -%}
        <p>
          <strong>WARNING:</strong> This product can expose you to chemicals
          including {{ chemical }}, which is known to the State of California to
          cause {{ harm }}. For more information go to
          <a href="https://www.P65Warnings.ca.gov" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">
            www.P65Warnings.ca.gov</a>.
        </p>
      {%- else -%}
        <p>
          <strong>WARNING:</strong> This product can expose you to chemicals which
          are known to the State of California to cause {{ harm }}. For more
          information go to
          <a href="https://www.P65Warnings.ca.gov" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">
            www.P65Warnings.ca.gov</a>.
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </details>
{%- endif -%}
